# Styling & Components

- Use ONLY Tailwind utility classes for layout and spacing
- Use Shadcn UI components for interactive elements (buttons, forms, cards, etc.)
- Never write custom CSS
- Use configured typography scale and semantic theme from globals.css
- Use '@tabler/icons-react' for icons

# Shadcn UI

- Always use Shadcn components when appropriate (Button, Card, Input, etc.)
- Install components as needed: `npx shadcn@latest add [component-name]`
- Import from @/components/ui/[component-name]
- Use Shadcn's built-in variants (default, secondary, destructive, outline, ghost, link)
- Extend variants in component files if needed for custom styles

# Available Shadcn Components

- Before using, check if installed.
- If not installed, suggest installation command

# Next.js & React

- Prefer Server Components (no 'use client' unless needed)

# Design-to-Code Workflow (MCP)

- When I provide a Penpot URL, ALWAYS use the Penpot MCP tools to inspect the design before writing code.

# Coding Standards

- Use TypeScript for all components.
- If a component requires state, use functional components with Hooks.
- For complex layouts, prioritize CSS Grid/Flexbox as defined in the Penpot file.
- Inspect design token defined in the Penpot and apply the closest global.css variables or Tailwind equivalent.
- Do not hallucinate properties; if a Penpot value is missing, ask me or use the closest Tailwind equivalent.

# Do NOT

- Add comments explaining obvious code
- Add features not requested
- Use external libraries beyond what's installed (Next.js, Tailwind, Shadcn, Tabler Icons)
- Use raw hex code or pixel measurement for styling
- Create additional components unless asked

